Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library cjson using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

You should invoke the functions in the following order: `cJSON_CreateObject` -> `cJSON_AddTrueToObject` -> `cJSON_Delete`

Below is the detailed information:

1. `cJSON_AddTrueToObject`
​ Adds a JSON boolean `true` member to an object. Use with a valid `cJSON` object and key name; it creates a true item, inserts it, and returns it on success. If insertion fails, it deletes the item and returns `NULL`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON*)
cJSON_AddTrueToObject(cJSON* const object, const char* const name);
​ ```
2. `cJSON_CreateObject`
​ `cJSON_CreateObject()` allocates a new empty `cJSON` item and marks it as `cJSON_Object`. Use it as the root or a child object, then add members with cJSON add APIs. Returns `NULL` if allocation fails.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON *)
cJSON_CreateObject(void);
​ ```
3. `cJSON_Delete`
​ Deletes a cJSON item and all owned descendants. Call it on a root node when done. It walks `next` siblings, frees `child`, `valuestring`, and `string` unless marked `cJSON_IsReference`/`cJSON_StringIsConst`, then frees each node.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Delete a cJSON entity and all subentities. */
CJSON_PUBLIC(void)
cJSON_Delete(cJSON *item);
​ ```

## Related Data Types

```c
/* The cJSON structure: */
struct cJSON {
 /* next/prev allow you to walk array/object chains. Alternatively, use GetArraySize/GetArrayItem/GetObjectItem */
 struct cJSON *next;
 struct cJSON *prev;
 /* An array or object item will have a child pointer pointing to a chain of the items in the array/object. */
 struct cJSON *child;

 /* The type of the item, as above. */
 int type;

 /* The item's string, if type==cJSON_String and type == cJSON_Raw */
 char *valuestring;
 /* writing to valueint is DEPRECATED, use cJSON_SetNumberValue instead */
 int valueint;
 /* The item's number, if type==cJSON_Number */
 double valuedouble;

 /* The item's name string, if this item is the child of, or is in the list of subitems of an object. */
 char *string;
} cJSON;

/* The cJSON structure: */
typedef struct cJSON cJSON;
```

## Required Header Files

You need to include `cJSON.h` to invoke functions above.
