Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library cjson using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `cJSON_ReplaceItemViaPointer`
​ Replaces `item` in `parent` with `replacement` using pointers, preserving list order and shifting later items right. Use only when `item` is already a child of `parent`. Returns `true` on success; `false` if args are NULL. If `replacement==item`, it’s a no-op and returns `true`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Shifts pre-existing items to the right. */
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_ReplaceItemViaPointer(cJSON* const parent, cJSON* const item, cJSON* replacement);
​ ```
2. `cJSON_DetachItemViaPointer`
​ Detaches `item` from `parent`’s array/object without deleting it. Use only with a child of `parent`; it returns the detached node or `NULL` if `parent/item` is `NULL` or `item` isn’t linked to `parent`. It fixes sibling links and clears parent links.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Remove/Detach items from Arrays/Objects. */
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON *)
cJSON_DetachItemViaPointer(cJSON *parent, cJSON *const item);
​ ```
3. `cJSON_ReplaceItemInArray`
​ Replaces the array element at index `which` with `newitem`. Use on a cJSON array with `which >= 0`; it looks up the item and delegates replacement by pointer. Returns `false` for negative index or if replacement fails.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_ReplaceItemInArray(cJSON *array, int which, cJSON *newitem);
​ ```
4. `cJSON_InsertItemInArray`
​ Inserts `newitem` into `array` at index `which`. Use with a valid array and non-NULL item; negative index fails. If `which` is past the end, it appends. Returns false on invalid/corrupt array state, otherwise links the item into the list.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Update array items. */
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_InsertItemInArray(cJSON *array, int which, cJSON *newitem);
​ ```
5. `cJSON_AddItemToArray`
​ `cJSON_AddItemToArray` appends an existing `cJSON` item to a JSON array. Use it after creating/parsing the item. It returns `true` on success, `false` if the array/item is invalid or insertion fails.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Append item to the specified array/object. */
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_AddItemToArray(cJSON *array, cJSON *item);
​ ```
6. `cJSON_IsObject`
​ `cJSON_IsObject` checks whether a `cJSON*` is a non-NULL JSON object. Use it before treating an item as an object. It returns `false` for `NULL` or any non-object type, and `true` only when `(item->type & 0xFF) == cJSON_Object`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_IsObject(const cJSON* const item);
​ ```

## Related Data Types

```c
