 * WARNING: When this function was used, make sure to always check that (item->type & cJSON_StringIsConst) is zero before
 * writing to `item->string` */
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_AddItemToObjectCS(cJSON *object, const char *string, cJSON *item);
​ ```
3. `cJSON_Print`
​ `cJSON_Print` renders a `cJSON` value into a newly allocated, pretty-printed JSON text string using the global hooks. Use it on a valid `cJSON*`; the caller owns the returned `char*` and must free it. Returns `NULL` on failure.
​ Its signature is:
