5. `cJSON_AddItemToObject`
​ Adds `item` to a JSON object under key `string`. Use it with an object node and a valid `cJSON*` item; it returns `cJSON_bool`. It delegates to internal `add_item_to_object(...)` with global hooks and `false` for the last flag.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_AddItemToObject(cJSON *object, const char *string, cJSON *item);
​ ```
6. `cJSON_InitHooks`
​ Sets cJSON’s global allocators. Pass `hooks` to override malloc/free; `realloc` is enabled only when both custom hooks are absent (default malloc/free). Pass `NULL` to reset to standard `malloc/free/realloc`.
